"models/student.py": {
  role: "Student model",
  summary: `The Student class: id, name, email, password and a list of Subject objects. It converts itself to a dictionary for the file (convert_to_file_data) and is rebuilt from a dictionary (create_from_file_data).`,
  why: `The file stores plain dictionaries (JSON). The program prefers real objects. These two methods translate between the two.`,
  say: `Student is a model class. In memory a student holds real Subject objects. To save, convert_to_file_data turns it into a dictionary that JSON can store. To load, create_from_file_data, a class method, builds a Student back from that dictionary.`,
  notes: [
    [1, 1, "subject_from_dict", `Imports the helper that turns a subject dictionary into a Subject object.`, `Needed when loading a student from the file.`, {d: `models/subject.py`}],
    [2, 2, "class Student", `Starts the Student class (a blueprint for student objects).`, ``],
    [3, 3, "def __init__", `The constructor. Runs when you write Student(...). Takes the id, name, email, password and an optional list of subjects.`, `subjects=None is used instead of subjects=[] on purpose: a [] default would be SHARED by every student (a classic Python trap).`, {i: `student_id, name, email, password, subjects (optional)`}],
    [4, 7, "self.student_id", `Saves each value on the object (self) so other methods can use it later.`, ``],
    [8, 8, "self.subjects =", `If subjects were given, use them; otherwise start with a new empty list.`, `Each student gets their OWN list.`, {s: `I use None as the default and create a new list inside, so two students never share the same subject list.`}],
    [10, 10, "def convert_to_file_data", `Method that turns this Student into a plain dictionary.`, `json.dumps cannot save custom objects, only dicts, lists, strings and numbers.`, {o: `a dict with keys id, name, email, password, subjects`}],
    [12, 14, "subject_dicts", `Loops over every Subject object and calls subject.to_dict() to get a dictionary for each.`, `Subjects must also be converted before saving.`],
    [15, 23, "return {", `Returns the dictionary. Note the key is "id" in the file but "student_id" on the object. The old line (commented out) saved Subject objects directly, which would fail.`, `This is the exact shape stored in students.data.`],
    [25, 26, "@classmethod", `A class method: it is called on the class (Student.create_from_file_data(data)), receives the class as cls, and returns a NEW Student.`, `A second way to build a Student, from file data. This is sometimes called a "factory" method.`, {i: `student_data (a dict from the file)`, o: `a Student object`}],
    [28, 30, "subject_objects", `Turns each subject dictionary back into a Subject object using subject_from_dict().`, ``],
    [31, 39, "return cls(", `Calls the constructor with the values read from the dictionary.`, ``],
  ],
},

