"admin_system/admin_controller.py": {
  role: "Admin logic",
  summary: `Two helper functions (generate_output_string_from_students, calculate_average_mark_and_grade) and the AdminController class: clear_database, group_students, partition_student, remove_student, show_students.`,
  why: `All admin features from the assignment live here.`,
  say: `The admin controller works on the student dictionaries from the database. For each student it calculates the average mark of their subjects and the grade for that average. Group puts students into Z, P, C, D, HD lists. Partition splits them into PASS (50 or more) and FAIL.`,
  notes: [
    [1, 8, "from database.database import Database", `Imports Database (used as a type hint), calculate_grade, the constants and the admin errors.`, ``],
    [10, 23, "def generate_output_string_from_students", `Builds one long text like "John Smith :: 673358 --> GRADE: C - MARK: 68.25, ...". After the loop it removes the last ", " with [:-2].`, `Shared by group, partition and show so the format is the same everywhere.`, {i: `list of student dicts`, o: `string`, s: `I build the string in a loop and then cut off the last comma and space with [:-2].`}],
    [28, 42, "def calculate_average_mark_and_grade", `Adds up the marks of all subjects and divides by the number of subjects. A student with no subjects gets 0.0 (to avoid dividing by zero). Returns (average, grade) as a pair (tuple).`, `It does not write into the student dict, because get_all_students() returns the live records and anything added would be saved to the file.`, {i: `student dict`, o: `(average_mark, grade) e.g. (68.25, "C")`, s: `I check for zero subjects first, because dividing by zero would crash. Those students get 0.0, which is a Z and a FAIL.`, w: `The average is not rounded, so a student with marks 70, 70, 71 shows MARK: 70.33333333333333.`}],
    [44, 46, "class AdminController", `Stores the shared database.`, ``],
    [48, 54, "def clear_database", `Deletes all students and prints "successfully cleared database".`, ``],
    [56, 63, "def group_students", `Prints "GRADE GROUPING". If there are no students prints "<Nothing to display>".`, ``],
    [65, 83, "z_students = []", `Five empty lists. For each student, compute the average and add the student to the right list using the same bands as calculate_grade.`, `Grouping by AVERAGE grade, as the sample output shows.`],
    [85, 103, "if len(z_students) > 0", `Prints only the groups that have students, e.g. "C --> [John Smith :: 673358 --> GRADE: C - MARK: 68.25]".`, ``, {w: `Line 87 prints "Z -- > [" with an extra space, while the others print "P --> [". A small inconsistency an instructor might spot.`}],
    [106, 108, "except Exception as e", `Any error: print it and raise GroupStudentsError.`, ``],
    [110, 124, "def partition_student", `Prints "PASS/FAIL PARTITIONING". Average below 50 -> fail list, otherwise pass list.`, ``],
    [126, 134, "fail_output_string", `Prints "FAIL --> [...]" then "PASS --> [...]". Empty lists still print "[]".`, `Matches the sample, which always shows both lines.`],
    [140, 150, "def remove_student", `Looks up the student by ID. If missing prints "Student does not exist", otherwise deletes it.`, ``, {w: `On success it prints NOTHING. Check your assignment sample: if it expects a message like "Removing Student <id> Account", this is a gap.`}],
    [152, 162, "def show_students", `Prints all students in one list, or "<Nothing to display>".`, ``],
  ],
},

