"student_system/student_controller.py": {
  role: "Student logic: validation, register, login",
  summary: `StudentController checks email/password format with regex, creates unique 6-digit IDs, registers new students, and logs students in for the CLI (login) and GUI (login_gui).`,
  why: `All student account rules in one class.`,
  say: `StudentController handles accounts. It checks the email and password against the regex in constants.py. Register refuses an email that already exists, asks for a name, gives a random unique 6-digit ID and saves. Login finds the student by email, checks the password and returns a Student object.`,
  notes: [
    [1, 2, "import random", `random for IDs, re for regular expressions.`, ``],
    [4, 12, "from models.student import Student", `Imports Student, the constants and exceptions.`, ``],
    [15, 17, "RED =", `ANSI colour codes. Printing "\\033[91m" turns terminal text red, "\\033[0m" resets it.`, `Makes error messages red and info yellow, like the sample output.`],
    [20, 22, "class StudentController", `Stores the database.`, ``],
    [24, 27, "def is_valid_credentials", `re.match returns a match object or None. "is not None" turns that into True/False. Both must be True.`, `One function for the format check used by login and register.`, {i: `email, password`, o: `True or False`}],
    [29, 38, "def ask_for_valid_credentials", `Keeps asking for Email and Password until both formats are valid. Then prints "email and password formats acceptable" (yellow) and returns them. Wrong format prints "Incorrect email or password format" (red).`, ``, {w: `There is no way to cancel: the loop repeats until valid input is typed.`}],
    [40, 44, "def generate_unique_id", `Random number 1-999999, formatted with :06d to 6 digits with leading zeros (e.g. 42 -> "000042"). If that ID already exists, try again.`, `IDs must be unique.`, {s: `The f-string format :06d pads the number to six digits. The loop guarantees the ID is not already used.`}],
    [46, 53, "def register", `Prints "Student Sign Up", gets valid credentials, then checks the email. If it exists prints "Student <name> already exists" and returns.`, `No duplicate accounts.`],
    [55, 57, "name = \"\"", `Asks for Name until it is not empty.`, ``],
    [59, 64, "new_student = Student(", `Creates a Student with a new ID and no subjects, converts it to a dict and saves it with create_student. Prints "Enrolling Student <name>". If saving fails, catches CreateStudentError.`, ``],
    [66, 75, "def login", `Prints "Student Sign In", gets valid credentials, finds the student by email. If no student OR wrong password prints "Student does not exist" and returns None. Otherwise returns a Student object built from the file data.`, ``, {o: `Student or None`, w: `A wrong password also says "Student does not exist". This hides which part was wrong (good for security) but may confuse the user.`}],
    [77, 96, "def login_gui", `GUI version. Raises a specific error for empty fields, bad email format, or no match, then catches ALL of them and returns a pair: (Student, None) on success or (None, LoginGUIError) on failure.`, `Intended to give the GUI a result plus an error.`, {w: `LoginWindow.login() treats the RETURN VALUE as the Student and expects specific exceptions to be raised. They never are. Verified by running the code with a stand-in Tkinter: every login (good or bad) hides the login window and passes a tuple to EnrolmentWindow, which then fails. See the "GUI login issue" lesson.`}],
  ],
},

"student_system/enrolment_controller.py": {
  role: "Enrolment logic for one logged-in student",
  summary: `EnrolmentController holds one Student and the Database. It can list/count subjects, enrol (max 4), remove by ID, change password, and save the student back to the file.`,
  why: `Shared by BOTH the CLI EnrolmentMenu and the GUI EnrolmentWindow, so the rules are identical.`,
  say: `EnrolmentController has the enrolment rules. enrol() first checks the limit of 4 and raises EnrolmentLimitError. It then creates a subject with a unique random ID and random mark, adds it, and saves straight away. remove() pads the ID so 97 matches 097. After every change save_student converts the Student to a dict and calls update_student.`,
  notes: [
    [1, 3, "#handles", `Comments describing the purpose.`, ``],
    [5, 9, "from models.subject import", `Imports create_new_subject, pad_id and the two enrolment errors.`, ``],
    [11, 11, "MAX_SUBJECTS = 4", `The limit of 4 subjects per student.`, ``, {w: `Duplicates SubjectConstants.MAX_SUBJECTS in constants.py.`}],
    [16, 19, "class EnrolmentController", `Constructor stores the Student object and the Database.`, ``],
    [20, 25, "def get_subjects", `get_subjects returns the list of Subject objects. count_subjects returns how many.`, ``],
    [31, 37, "def enrol", `If the student already has 4 or more subjects, raise EnrolmentLimitError with the message "Students are allowed to enrol in 4 subjects only."`, `Checking the rule FIRST means nothing changes when the limit is reached.`, {s: `The limit is checked before anything changes, so a fifth subject is never added.`}],
    [40, 42, "existing_ids = []", `Collects the IDs the student already has.`, `So the new random ID is different.`],
    [44, 45, "create_new_subject", `Creates the new Subject and appends it to the student's list.`, ``],
    [48, 49, "self.save_student()", `Saves to students.data immediately, then returns the new subject so the menu can print its ID.`, ``, {o: `Subject`}],
    [51, 54, "def remove", `Pads the typed ID to 3 characters (97 -> "097").`, `Users may type without leading zeros.`],
    [58, 61, "subject_to_remove = None", `Searches the student's subjects for the matching ID.`, ``],
    [63, 66, "if subject_to_remove is None", `Not found -> raise SubjectNotFoundError("Subject <id> does not exist").`, ``],
    [67, 70, "self.student.subjects.remove", `Removes the subject from the list and saves.`, ``],
    [72, 74, "def change_password", `Sets the new password on the Student and saves.`, `The menu has already checked the format.`],
    [76, 82, "def save_student", `Converts the Student to a dict and calls database.update_student with the student's ID.`, `The single place where enrolment changes reach the file.`],
    [84, 88, "def get_student_id", `Small "getter" methods used by the GUI enrolment window.`, ``],
  ],
},

